{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean","id":954226,"title":"Potential exploit of Protean.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-19T22:25:59-07:00","id":954226,"title":"Potential exploit of Protean.","content":"Just had an idea. Could a Gangrel (or anyone with Protean 1) use Unmarked Grave to travel through walls/relatively thin barriers (assuming it isn't abnormally thick)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T22:31:01-07:00","id":954227,"title":"","content":"From the wording of the power, it seems like it's only intended to work on the ground, not on walls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T23:17:43-07:00","id":954247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954227#post954227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the wording of the power, it seems like it's only intended to work on the ground, not on walls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, always took it as being able to meld into whatever substance, the cost just dependent on the durability. Didn't matter if it was under you or if you were pressed up against it. But okay, if it is that way, then could a kindred use that ability to drop into an apartment below them? I.e. they are in the fourth floor, then use Unmarked Grave to meld into the concrete (at least for newer buildings), then pop out on the other side/from the ceiling? Or is it so that you come out of the exact same spot that you entered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T23:47:16-07:00","id":954253,"title":"","content":"I'd allow it as a devotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T01:29:48-07:00","id":954272,"title":"","content":"I think that you could even meld in a wall but not to going to the other side. You meld with the wall and become part of it, then you can't move wothout a devotion so you should get out from the same place you melded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T05:39:49-07:00","id":954316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954247#post954247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, always took it as being able to meld into whatever substance, the cost just dependent on the durability. Didn't matter if it was under you or if you were pressed up against it. But okay, if it is that way, then could a kindred use that ability to drop into an apartment below them? I.e. they are in the fourth floor, then use Unmarked Grave to meld into the concrete (at least for newer buildings), then pop out on the other side/from the ceiling? Or is it so that you come out of the exact same spot that you entered?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, cause the floor between apartments wouldn't be thick enough. Gotta be at least the same size as the vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T05:53:41-07:00","id":954324,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there a devotion in 1e that let you do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T06:01:05-07:00","id":954331,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a fantastic devotion, but raw doesnt work with protean 1","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T07:02:53-07:00","id":954356,"title":"","content":"<br /> I would never allow a vampire to merge with a floor or a wall and this is why: They mention the ground 9 times in the description of the first dot. Also no floor or wall is the same size as a human ( tall maybe, not wide ) like Charliquin pointed out. <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot; She merges with the <b>ground</b>, becoming<br /> immune to almost any harm. She can remain there indefinitely,<br /> waiting in a cocoon of <b>soil </b>until the time is right for her to<br /> emerge.<br /> <br /> <b>Requirement: The vampire\u2019s hiding place must be at least<br /> the same Size as her.</b><br /> <br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Duration: Indefinite<br /> <br /> The vampire sinks bodily into the <b>earth</b>, for as long as she<br /> desires. Once interred, she\u2019s mostly insensible to the outside<br /> world, though she can remain conscious if she so wishes.<br /> She has a sense of the <b>ground </b>above her \u2014 she\u2019s well aware if<br /> someone tries to <b>concrete over</b> her hiding place. Her Kindred<br /> senses continue to function, and she remains capable of sensing<br /> the predatory aura even though her safe haven means another<br /> vampire\u2019s predatory aura can\u2019t force her into a fight-or-flight<br /> reaction. Should someone spill blood or Vitae upon the <b>ground</b>,<br /> she can absorb it. The <b>ground </b>dilutes Vitae enough that it can\u2019t<br /> result in a blood bond, but to a Vitae-addicted vampire just the<br /> taste might be enough to drive her <b>out of the ground</b>, thirsty<br /> for more.<br /> The only way to harm the vampire is to damage or destroy the<br /> <b>ground she resides in;</b> she takes one point of bashing damage for<br /> each point of Structure that her haven loses. When she takes<br /> her first point of lethal damage she emerges from the ground,<br /> unable to hold herself in. &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T07:07:09-07:00","id":954358,"title":"","content":"Hmm, so is it more like a vertical grave then? Them &quot;standing&quot; in it? Always pictured them just sort of melting into the material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T07:29:17-07:00","id":954369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954358#post954358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, so is it more like a vertical grave then? Them &quot;standing&quot; in it? Always pictured them just sort of melting into the material.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It doesnt mention material. It mentions ground. Then it says you need to spend vitae to go through concrete or something. but you go through it to the ground<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T07:55:36-07:00","id":954381,"title":"","content":"Starting from the point that protean modify your own body and not the material, even if from the description it could be read also in this way, I think that you can meld your body in any material if its size is greater then yours as a wall is. I mean, the vampire's body merge in the wall and if it is to thiny she behaves like water in a paper towels. I can't think it's limited just to horizontal material.<br /> The book say &quot;ground&quot; becouse the power is born to meld vampire in the ground but I don't think is &quot;illegal&quot; using it for vertical surfaces. Because the only real difference is the orientation of the surface.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-20-2016, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T08:02:22-07:00","id":954383,"title":"","content":"I agree that the RAW seems to be as Vitalis and others have said. I am sympathetic, having thought that exploit was cannon but rules are rules.<br /> <br /> That said, one nitpick:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954356#post954356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Requirement: The vampire\u2019s hiding place must be at least<br /> the same Size as her.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Size here has a capital S and therefore indicates the variable, not a general reference.<br /> <br /> Page 182 of Blood and Smoke, while talking about objects, indicates that a door is Size 5. So it would appear to me that the 'wall-thickness' argument is a presumption not explicit in the text, as a Door is certainly only as thick as the wall.<br /> <br /> The intent of this requirement is unknown to me, but it seems plausible that it was to prevent Gangrel melding with small objects ('Elder in a coin' would be a funny devotion).<br /> <br /> That said, it is also likely that the intent of the requirement matches the presumption of the 'wall-thickness' argument and this is an innocent inconsistency between RAI and RAW. The 'ground-argument' makes this more plausible than not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":".  I am biologically unable to post with correct spelling the first time around. 08-20-2016, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T08:25:17-07:00","id":954394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954369#post954369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It doesnt mention material. It mentions ground. Then it says you need to spend vitae to go through concrete or something. but you go through it to the ground</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, so the vitae cost is to literally go through the material into the soil beneath it. Thought it was to go into it. Think in 1e you could go into different substances (i.e. water, wood, stone). I think, at least for the water one, that's where I'm getting mixed up, seeming like you wouldn't necessarily need a pool of water that is six feet deep, but maybe only 2 feet, so long as that if the vampire where to lie down in it, they would be completely submerged. <br /> <br /> <br /> So a quick question then, is it RAW that the size of the hiding place must be vertical? Could it not be a size 5 thing (example, garden bed in a shopping centre) that is laid out horizontally, and the vampire lies down before using Unmarked Grave?<br /> <br /> <br /> Quick edit: in 2e, it states &quot;She does not have to find stone or mud, she can just as easily slip into concrete&quot;. <br /> Stating that she slips INTO concrete, not through it into soil. And if she can easily slip into concrete, is it not much of a stretch to believe they could do other material as well? Assuming it is of correct size of course.<br /> <br /> Also note, that I am in no means challenging what it says in RAW to suit my purposes. It's more of an inquisitive nature. I'm aware that it can always be house-ruled otherwise, just curious as to what extent in RAW could be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3268,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","user":"Krzyzstof","date":". 08-20-2016, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T08:33:08-07:00","id":954403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954383#post954383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that the RAW seems to be as Vitalis and others have said. I am sympathetic, having thought that exploit was cannon but rules are rules.<br /> <br /> That said, one nitpick:<br /> <br /> <br /> Size here has a capital S and therefore indicates the variable, not a general reference.<br /> <br /> Page 182 of Blood and Smoke, while talking about objects, indicates that a door is Size 5. So it would appear to me that the 'wall-thickness' argument is a presumption not explicit in the text, as a Door is certainly only as thick as the wall.<br /> <br /> The intent of this requirement is unknown to me, but it seems plausible that it was to prevent Gangrel melding with small objects ('Elder in a coin' would be a funny devotion).<br /> <br /> That said, it is also likely that the intent of the requirement matches the presumption of the 'wall-thickness' argument and this is an innocent inconsistency between RAI and RAW. The 'ground-argument' makes this more plausible than not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> True, but for wall thickness that only really applies to internal walls. Exterior walls are more than thick enough for a person to hide in. In apartment buildings, most walls separating the various apartments are as thick, or close to, exterior walls. Especially vertically (i.e. floor/ceiling), if the body where placed horizontally. Now true, of his not the case for all apartment buildings/condos, but it is for a lot of the newer ones. But, how I thought of it, was that it didn't necessarily need to be as thick if it were a larger object. For an example we will keep with an internal wall. While yes, it maybe only be about 6 inches thick, but they are also usually at least 8 feet high, and 16 feet wide. So instead of being put in the wall (i know it's not exactly that way, but for arguments sake it seems like that is the best way to describe it), the kindred spreads out across this space.<br /> <br /> Maybe it could be a devotion using Protean 4 (thinking of the rubbery skin, maybe it could be stretched out to make the character fit in more areas).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3268,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","user":"Krzyzstof","date":". 08-20-2016, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:22:21-07:00","id":954474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954383#post954383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that the RAW seems to be as Vitalis and others have said. I am sympathetic, having thought that exploit was cannon but rules are rules.<br /> <br /> That said, one nitpick:<br /> <br /> <br /> Size here has a capital S and therefore indicates the variable, not a general reference.<br /> <br /> Page 182 of Blood and Smoke, while talking about objects, indicates that a door is Size 5. So it would appear to me that the 'wall-thickness' argument is a presumption not explicit in the text, as a Door is certainly only as thick as the wall.<br /> <br /> The intent of this requirement is unknown to me, but it seems plausible that it was to prevent Gangrel melding with small objects ('Elder in a coin' would be a funny devotion).<br /> <br /> That said, it is also likely that the intent of the requirement matches the presumption of the 'wall-thickness' argument and this is an innocent inconsistency between RAI and RAW. The 'ground-argument' makes this more plausible than not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with you. The intent of the size requirement is, according to me, to prevent a gangrel to meld into a flower pot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T11:17:19-07:00","id":954504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954474#post954474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree with you. The intent of the size requirement is, according to me, to prevent a gangrel to meld into a flower pot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree. My question is can they meld into material/substance/locations that aren't size 5 in a vertical sense. Or, can they spread themselves thin over a larger area. It doesn't quite say how a kindred merges with the ground other than &quot;... the earth itself yawns open to embrace the vampire.&quot;. So, are they just themselves but within the ground? Then that's more buried than merged. If it is literally turning into that substance, do they stay the same shape/size as when in human form? I am very curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T11:33:50-07:00","id":954511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954504#post954504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I completely agree. My question is can they meld into material/substance/locations that aren't size 5 in a vertical sense. Or, can they spread themselves thin over a larger area. It doesn't quite say how a kindred merges with the ground other than &quot;... the earth itself yawns open to embrace the vampire.&quot;. So, are they just themselves but within the ground? Then that's more buried than merged. If it is literally turning into that substance, do they stay the same shape/size as when in human form? I am very curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>How I said, reading the book, it'd seems that the matters open to embrace the vampire body, but personally I see protean as a shapeshifting discipline. Is the body of the vampire that change, like in the first edition was clearely specified, not the matter around him. So, if you see the power like me, I would say, yes, the vampire can spread also in thiny vertical wall. The complessive size must be 5 or more without specification about width and height.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T18:35:22-07:00","id":954717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954504#post954504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I completely agree. My question is can they meld into material/substance/locations that aren't size 5 in a vertical sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>My whole point was that the rule applied to the stat called Size, not what the word 'size' might mean. There is no such thing as vertical size. There is Size, and an object has a number to represent it. As a door is Size 5 and is no thicker than a wall, then walls ought not to be a problem, no matter what, according to RAW. A wall likely has greater Size, and so further discussion is moot.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:25:33-07:00","id":954822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954717#post954717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My whole point was that the rule applied to the stat called Size, not what the word 'size' might mean. There is no such thing as vertical size. There is Size, and an object has a number to represent it. As a door is Size 5 and is no thicker than a wall, then walls ought not to be a problem, no matter what, according to RAW. A wall likely has greater Size, and so further discussion is moot.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Walls are only &quot;not a problem&quot; if you ignore the 9 times the description of the discipline references the ground. Walls are decidedly not the ground. Walls and doors and roofs are pretty much opposite of the ground and earth. Some floors, walls and doors don't even touch the ground or earth. <br /> <br /> The only way I would allow you to meld into a wall is if it were a cave wall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:46:18-07:00","id":954829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954822#post954822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Walls are only &quot;not a problem&quot; if you ignore the 9 times the description of the discipline references the ground. Walls are decidedly not the ground. Walls and doors and roofs are pretty much opposite of the ground and earth. Some floors, walls and doors don't even touch the ground or earth. <br /> <br /> The only way I would allow you to meld into a wall is if it were a cave wall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but it also clearly states that you can meld into concrete, and concrete doesn't necessarily need to be on the ground. Example being that a lot of really expensive condo buildings have concrete for walls and floor, separating the different condos as a way to help sound-proof each unit. At least it is happening in Toronto. Now, the fact that it states that you can meld into concrete, I would say it isn't a far stretch for the kindred to meld into other materials as I mentioned earlier/like in 1E Protean. Now, I re-read 1E Protean, and it actually mentions that if you use it in water, there is an almost shimmer-like image of yourself that can be seen if looked at closely. So that does make me think that, regardless of the size of the material, you need to be able to be contained within it in some manner. Either standing/laying down/fetal position/whatever.<br /> <br /> So, so I suppose a better question at this stage is, in Vampire 2e, can a kindred using Protean 1, meld into other materials other than soil. It states that they can meld into concrete, but is that more of the kindred passing through the concrete into the soil beneath (assuming that there is any)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:54:20-07:00","id":954832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954829#post954829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, but it also clearly states that you can meld into concrete, and concrete doesn't necessarily need to be on the ground. Example being that a lot of really expensive condo buildings have concrete for walls and floor, separating the different condos as a way to help sound-proof each unit. At least it is happening in Toronto. Now, the fact that it states that you can meld into concrete, I would say it isn't a far stretch for the kindred to meld into other materials as I mentioned earlier/like in 1E Protean. Now, I re-read 1E Protean, and it actually mentions that if you use it in water, there is an almost shimmer-like image of yourself that can be seen if looked at closely. So that does make me think that, regardless of the size of the material, you need to be able to be contained within it in some manner. Either standing/laying down/fetal position/whatever.<br /> <br /> So, so I suppose a better question at this stage is, in Vampire 2e, can a kindred using Protean 1, meld into other materials other than soil. It states that they can meld into concrete, but is that more of the kindred passing through the concrete into the soil beneath (assuming that there is any)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Concrete can be the ground and a wall but since it says concrete and ground you would take something that fits both of those things, like a parking lot or road. When it has more than one requirement you have to make sure it fits both. <br /> <br /> For example: a triangle. All sides are equal. There is only one type of triangle that fits that, where there are 2 that don't. You can't just say all triangles fit because it says triangle. <br /> <br /> Protean was changed so much between first and second edition I would not compare too much... They aren't even the same level anymore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:57:18-07:00","id":954836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954832#post954832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Concrete can be the ground and a wall but since it says concrete and ground you would take something that fits both of those things, like a parking lot or road. When it has more than one requirement you have to make sure it fits both. <br /> <br /> For example: a triangle. All sides are equal. There is only one type of triangle that fits that, where there are 2 that don't. You can't just say all triangles fit because it says triangle. <br /> <br /> Protean was changed so much between first and second edition I would not compare too much... They aren't even the same level anymore</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree to that. Okay, so for this point, is ground listed as anything you stand on? Or all natural (as much as it can be these days) earth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T23:01:50-07:00","id":954842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954836#post954836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can agree to that. Okay, so for this point, is ground listed as anything you stand on? Or all natural (as much as it can be these days) earth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Anything you can stand on because that would include a floor on the 5th floor of a building. The ground would be any physical earth and after that.. Common sense. Parking lots, roads, caves, Brick patios, ect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T23:12:46-07:00","id":954850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954842#post954842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not Anything you can stand on because that would include a floor on the 5th floor of a building. The ground would be any physical earth and after that.. Common sense. Parking lots, roads, caves, Brick patios, ect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wanted to confirm that it was listed directly as earth/soil. Although I wonder if a loop hole could be used. Transport a crate of dirt roughly 6-feet tall, 3-4 feet wide. Might make for an interesting way to transport kindred without using coffins. Although what would happen if the box broke? Just, forced out of slumber?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T05:02:01-07:00","id":954908,"title":"","content":"I don't think interpreting rules literally should come at the expense of a good story. The inclusion of concrete was a nod to foundations which are not necessarily at ground level. The key points seem to be the structure has one clear point to meld in and out, the structure is at least as large as the vampire, and the structure can't be moved. A wall, or ceiling, should be fine as long as it fits the same conditions. There are inherent disadvantages to not sticking with the floor, usually the last thing ever touched.<br /> <br /> I would not allow for melding through anything with unmarked grave because the intent is to create a hiding place. Primeval Miasma, or a variant, should be used to go through something. That would be the power with the proper intent.<br /> <br /> For transport, I would suggest a Protean/Vigor devotion that allows for melding into the floors of ships, train cars, or airplanes. I would stick to more or less the same spot would be used to exit as enter. The added boost of power makes up for the fact that the structure moves. The idea is too good let technicalities get in the way. Protean 1 / Vigor / Obfusctate 5 for the vampire pirate's ghost ship is what I would be thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T07:09:08-07:00","id":954935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954908#post954908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think interpreting rules literally should come at the expense of a good story. The inclusion of concrete was a nod to foundations which are not necessarily at ground level. The key points seem to be the structure has one clear point to meld in and out, the structure is at least as large as the vampire, and the structure can't be moved. A wall, or ceiling, should be fine as long as it fits the same conditions. There are inherent disadvantages to not sticking with the floor, usually the last thing ever touched.<br /> <br /> I would not allow for melding through anything with unmarked grave because the intent is to create a hiding place. Primeval Miasma, or a variant, should be used to go through something. That would be the power with the proper intent.<br /> <br /> For transport, I would suggest a Protean/Vigor devotion that allows for melding into the floors of ships, train cars, or airplanes. I would stick to more or less the same spot would be used to exit as enter. The added boost of power makes up for the fact that the structure moves. The idea is too good let technicalities get in the way. Protean 1 / Vigor / Obfusctate 5 for the vampire pirate's ghost ship is what I would be thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that interpreting the rules for every day use should be a thing. We shouldn't just throw away rules because we don't like them. Or change them because we dont think it should work like that. The developers chose words and words all have connotations and denotations and any good writer knows that. There is a huge difference between walk and trot. and Earth and floor. and delicious and good. Yes some of the rules are vague and can be interpreted more than one way, but some of the rules are really clear that should not be open to interpretation. <br /> <br /> I think someone said in another thread that if we do change a rule we should say something like &quot;Yes normally that's the way it works, but this guy can do it differently. Dont you want to find out why?&quot; There is your plot hook, but it is no longer a plot hook if you globally change it to &quot;Yes all vampires do it this way, because I didnt like the RAW&quot; <br /> <br /> Diggs, if you could melt into a floor or a wall. Don't you feel that would have mentioned in stead of repeatedly mentioning the ground? Even if they just once changed ground to &quot;material&quot; or &quot;place&quot; or &quot;wood&quot;. I cant speak for the developers, but I strongly believe that instead of mentioning ground/earth 9 times they would have taken some of those and expanded their description to include a floor or plane instead of repeatedly beating it into our head that it is the ground. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=954850#post954850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just wanted to confirm that it was listed directly as earth/soil. Although I wonder if a loop hole could be used. Transport a crate of dirt roughly 6-feet tall, 3-4 feet wide. Might make for an interesting way to transport kindred without using coffins. Although what would happen if the box broke? Just, forced out of slumber?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say a giant crate of dirt would be just fine as it is a giant crate of earth. If the crate broke and the land was damage, see the rules for damaged land. Your character would be expelled from it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T10:58:49-07:00","id":955023,"title":"","content":"The floor was mentioned with &quot;she can just as easily slip into concrete&quot; unless you consider ground to be made of concrete. Ground is the generic term for what you are standing on. A highway overpass is the ground when you are on it. A bridge is the ground when you are on it. The description clearly allows for materials other than soil or earth which is the only thing the ground would be made of if you are going to be literal. Where do you get a plane from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T11:08:50-07:00","id":955027,"title":"","content":"I think Protean is only supposed to let you meld with &quot;earth&quot; which ranges from dirt to rock and concrete. I don't think metal qualifies as &quot;earth&quot;. I know in the 1e ventrue clanbook there was a bit where a ventrue with Protean slept inside a large stone statue inside his office.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T11:48:51-07:00","id":955050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=955023#post955023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The floor was mentioned with &quot;she can just as easily slip into concrete&quot; unless you consider ground to be made of concrete. Ground is the generic term for what you are standing on. A highway overpass is the ground when you are on it. A bridge is the ground when you are on it. The description clearly allows for materials other than soil or earth which is the only thing the ground would be made of if you are going to be literal. Where do you get a plane from?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps you and I differ on what &quot;ground&quot; is. Below is what I think it is. I think a paved parking lot is the ground. Where a road 30 feet above the ground is no longer ground. You're up in the air. the opposite of ground. Ground is not a generic term, it has a meaning. something attached to the earth. Stone is earth, rock is earth. Dirt is earth. Concrete is just earth that was unnaturally put somewhere, but still ground. a concrete parking garage 10 stories tall is not the ground. All that said, I think you and your table so do what makes you happy. Home brew it how ever you want<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u0261round<br /> <i>noun</i></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>1</b>.<br /> the solid surface of the earth.</span></span></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-21-2016, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:17:05-07:00","id":955068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.oxforddictionaries.com/definition/english/ground\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/languages.oup.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/OL-URL-thumbnail.png?fit=1200%2C627&amp;ssl=1\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.oxforddictionaries.com/definition/english/ground\" target=\"_blank\"> Oxford Languages </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.oxforddictionaries.com/definition/english/ground\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.oxforddictionaries.com/definition/english/ground </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The home of language data. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1.3 British The floor of a room:<br /> the device fell to the ground, where it exploded, blowing a hole in the floor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:21:15-07:00","id":955074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=955068#post955068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.oxforddictionaries.com/definition/english/ground\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.oxforddictionaries.com/de...english/ground</a><br /> <br /> <br /> 1.3 British The floor of a room:<br /> the device fell to the ground, where it exploded, blowing a hole in the floor</div> </div> </div> </div>British English and American English are not the same language.<br /> <br /> Therefore some words have different meanings. Like Flats are shoes in American English and Flats are apartments in British English.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-21-2016, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:01:27-07:00","id":955112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean#post954226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just had an idea. Could a Gangrel (or anyone with Protean 1) use Unmarked Grave to travel through walls/relatively thin barriers (assuming it isn't abnormally thick)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd allow it as a devotion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:03:06-07:00","id":955114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=955074#post955074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> British English and American English are not the same language.<br /> <br /> Therefore some words have different meanings. Like Flats are shoes in American English and Flats are apartments in British English.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've lived in America all my life, and I've heard ground used that way plenty.<br /> <br /> Also, technically they're not different languages, they're different dialects of the same language.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:19:21-07:00","id":955123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=955050#post955050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Perhaps you and I differ on what &amp;quot;ground&amp;quot; is. Below is what I think it is. I think a paved parking lot is the ground. Where a road 30 feet above the ground is no longer ground. You're up in the air. the opposite of ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if you are on the earth 100 yards above an hidden cave, you are not on the ground anymore? What's the difference with a bridge, considering that concrete is a legit place where to merge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:08:47-07:00","id":955164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=955114#post955114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've lived in America all my life, and I've heard ground used that way plenty.<br /> <br /> Also, technically they're not different languages, they're different dialects of the same language.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have lived in America my whole life too. And I have not heard the floor referred to as the ground. Floor and ground are not interchangeable words. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7079_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7079\" data-vbnamecard=\"7079\">Marcus</a> See my triangle example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-21-2016, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:12:10-07:00","id":955168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=955164#post955164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have lived in America my whole life too. And I have not heard the floor referred to as the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, so we've established that some Americans use that meaning of ground and some don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:42:20-07:00","id":955190,"title":"","content":"Does anyone use the term ground to refer to walls?<br /> <br /> Or have secrets in their game that would be ruined by someone's ability to break through a concrete ceiling, that is a floor, without the use of sledgehammers or other devices?<br /> <br /> Would your games be irrevocably broken with players having access to those secrets by means other than Dominating their way into a building, Obfuscating and sneaking in, even using Auspex to pry pass-codes from people inside, or using a variety of Skills and equipment at the PCs disposal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-21-2016, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T16:14:41-07:00","id":955267,"title":"","content":"protean 1 is a power who's entire thing is hiding you in a solid mass for safety and then spitting you out in the same place. It's not an at will Passwall spell. if you want to use it as such, you need to develop a devotion for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T17:47:54-07:00","id":955325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=955168#post955168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Great, so we've established that some Americans use that meaning of ground and some don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have any idea how many Americans say, &quot;I seen this&quot; or &quot;I seen that&quot; or how many don't know the difference between <i>there, their </i>and <i>they're</i>? My personal favorites the misuse of <i>Irregardless </i>or <i>dethaw. </i>Some of them are right, and some of them are wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T18:01:53-07:00","id":955331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=955325#post955325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have any idea how many Americans say, &quot;I seen this&quot; or &quot;I seen that&quot; or how many don't know the difference between <i>there, their </i>and <i>they're</i>? My personal favorites the misuse of <i>Irregardless </i>or <i>dethaw. </i>Some of them are right, and some of them are wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay? You're hanging your argument on a technical reading of the word ground in a game that's written in natural language, and when confronted with the fact that floor is a valid dictionary definition of the word you're trying to double down on your technical reading by arguing about dialects and natural language often being technically incorrect... Just... Seems like a strange hill to die on when there are better arguments to be made as to why the intent is probably for it to not work on suspended surfaces. Case in point, TidyGamer's post just above yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-21-2016, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:16:58-07:00","id":955664,"title":"","content":"I agree that the intention is probably not suspended surfaces otherwise if &quot;floor&quot; works, then why not meld into the &quot;floor&quot; of a car/bus/boat/airplane/spaceship?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:15:59-07:00","id":955773,"title":"","content":"The name of it seems to imply the Vampire can fuse with dirt to create a seamless &quot;grave&quot; for themselves to sleep in safely. Unless people are making graves out of concrete and/or putting them in walls, I'd say it was against concept. But perfectly in line with a low cost Devotion, as others have stated.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering what level of Protean, and potentially any other Disciplines, would be required to instead have a substance merge with you. Goal: power that gives the vampire a skin of stone (or concrete, etc.) to simulate turning into a stone Gargoyle to hide from the sun's rays (or operate with stone-skin armor at night).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T12:49:23-07:00","id":955817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=955773#post955773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless people are making graves out of concrete and/or putting them in walls, I'd say it was against concept. But perfectly in line with a low cost Devotion, as others have stated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what about cubicles in catacombs? They are litterally graves in the wall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:04:56-07:00","id":955877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=955773#post955773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering what level of Protean, and potentially any other Disciplines, would be required to instead have a substance merge with you. Goal: power that gives the vampire a skin of stone (or concrete, etc.) to simulate turning into a stone Gargoyle to hide from the sun's rays (or operate with stone-skin armor at night).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a Protean 4, Resilience something Devotion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=955817#post955817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, what about cubicles in catacombs? They are litterally graves in the wall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, Sarcophagi are stone as well. However, they are both for the VERY wealthy and not the masses. Which again brings us to the Devotion solution if you want to meld with any stonelike substance without it being in direct contact with the earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 08-22-2016, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:28:27-07:00","id":955891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=955773#post955773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The name of it seems to imply the Vampire can fuse with dirt to create a seamless &quot;grave&quot; for themselves to sleep in safely. Unless people are making graves out of concrete and/or putting them in walls, I'd say it was against concept. But perfectly in line with a low cost Devotion, as others have stated.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering what level of Protean, and potentially any other Disciplines, would be required to instead have a substance merge with you. Goal: power that gives the vampire a skin of stone (or concrete, etc.) to simulate turning into a stone Gargoyle to hide from the sun's rays (or operate with stone-skin armor at night).</div> </div> </div> </div>This already exists. Page 144, Gargoyle's Vigilance (advanced form) Protean 5, Auspex 1, Resilience 2, 5xp total for the devotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","name":"CrimsonOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T18:54:05-07:00","id":956062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/954226-potential-exploit-of-protean?p=955773#post955773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering what level of Protean, and potentially any other Disciplines, would be required to instead have a substance merge with you. Goal: power that gives the vampire a skin of stone (or concrete, etc.) to simulate turning into a stone Gargoyle to hide from the sun's rays (or operate with stone-skin armor at night).</div> </div> </div> </div>There is already a gargoyle Devotion in the book, though it doesn't really merge with a substance. Gargoyle's Vigilance with the Protean 5 option. Auspex 1 (which I imagine you could drop, or probably replace with a few dots of Vigor if you want to be able to move around), Resilience 2, Protean 5.<br /> <br /> Edit: And I just now see there was another page and someone got to it before me. Oh well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T19:55:43-07:00","id":956093,"title":"","content":"Noted. I was thinking of the Stone-skin as primary, and not a secondary option to a sensory power. Kinda surprised it requires Protean 5, though. I suppose that is necessary if you are turning into a statue outright (as opposed to just picking up a layer as a second skin).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T20:08:06-07:00","id":956099,"title":"","content":"Well, Protean 5 is the first full-body transformation into something not-flesh (mist). So that makes sense for a full-body stone transformation. For just skin, Unnatural Aspect might fit at 4 dots instead? with Resilience for the armor effect and either Vigor or Celerity for movement. I lean towards Vigor, since I can't imagine it being... fast, by any means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T14:23:26-07:00","id":956547,"title":"","content":"In case it was lost in the ground defining debate, my point was that Grave would not allow transport as it is beyond the scope of the power so no Pass Thru Walls. I would not allow switching floors in a cave system using Grave either.<br /> <br /> Walls are clearly not ground but as long as they were treated the same way as the ground then I don't see a problem. There is no advantage except surprise which I would then say you need a Devotion to create a variant power. Anyone that knows about Protean expects melding into the ground so when treating walls the same as ground then everyone would expect that too.<br /> <br /> My thinking is a use that does not fit the description but does fit the intended use without advantage is a reasonable expansion as long as it fits the general theme. If you wanted to meld into a tree that should be a variant instead of the normal power or a Devotion at the same level. Earth and trees would be different themes.<br /> <br /> Planes and trains move so I think you have to add Vigor to the Devotion as that is beyond the scope of the power as well. Moving a patch of dirt requires damaging it. Melding into a statue is something I would consider the same as a plane or train floor. I'm no good at creating Devotions, but I think it should be Protean 1 and Vigor at 1 or 2. This would be melding with an existing statue the same size as the vampire.<br /> <br /> Vigor is the standard discipline to add to a Devotion to boost a power while keeping it in the same general vein. At least, that has been the direction development has taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}